VAN DOORN & HOWARD'S
NEW CROCKERY STORE.
To keep up the excitement, just for the fun of it,
going to show the citizens of this and adjoining that
is not so "prosperous" to keep Crockery Store
alone as would think for the proof of which call and
examine the prices of articles in the following
ware, such

Baking Napels, fire proof;

Enamelled, Brown and White Pie Plates;
Brown and White Pudding Pans;

Striped and White Lip Bowls;

White and Yellow Bakers, all sizes;

Pitchers, Mugs and Cups—we have endless number of
styles, shapes, colors and SIZES;

brown, White and Enamelled Cake Jars;

Bread Bowls that will hold half bushel;
White and Enamelled Soap Dishes;

Soap Slabs in any quantity to suit customers;
Birds Baths and Cups Platters in all sizes;
Bed Pans, Chambers, Stop Jars, Foot Baths, &c. too
numerous to MENTION;

Warming Jugs for sick people;

Pitchers with holes in the bottom, something new, that
will hold water forever and not leak;

Common Tea Sets for sick;

Rockingham Teapots, Spoons, jugs and other
articles too numerous to mention.

TO BE CONTINUED.
Persons in any the above articles buy them
cheaper at the New Crockery Store, than at other
firms in the State. VAN DOORN & HOWARD.
